'' STR( ) OF AN ENUM AS THE LEFT TERM OF A CONCATENATION PRINTS. 'print str( V2.d ) &
'' " z"' printed nothing, where fbc prints "2 z", and tiko said nothing -- --dump-ir
'' counted the line among its "statements not lowered". Check does not type a '&' chain,
'' so PRINT classifies one by its LEFT term, and ExprIntrinsicType_ (intrinsics.bas) left
'' str( ) of an enum UNTYPED: its argument had no builtin type, so it was not "numeric".
'' 'print str( V2.d )' alone and 'dim s as string = str( V2.d ) & ...' were unaffected --
'' one has its own path, the other is typed by its destination. The same rule typed hex,
'' oct, bin, space, sgn, sin, sqr, atan2, mkl, chr and bit, and each declined the same way.
''
'' RUN, because the failure was a missing line: nothing in a dump or a link shows it.
'' The source is also a goldenrun.sh differential -- byte-identical to fbc's build.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/enum-str-concat.bas -o tests/driver/enumstrconcat.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/enumstrconcat.exe
'' RUN: tests/driver/enumstrconcat.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2 z
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2 w
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 1 y
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2 ev
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 1 cv
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2 hx
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2 oc
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 10 bn
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2 sp
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 1 sg
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 0.9092974268256817 sn
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 1.414213562373095 sq
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 0.7853981633974483 at
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 4 mk
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 65 ch
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: -1 bt
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 6 bs
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2!
